    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense, I'll try using a shim to help distribute the tension. I'm also wondering if there's anything else I might be overlooking regarding the physical properties of the walnut itself. Sometimes it feels like the wood is just... unpredictable, like it's resisting the cut in a way that doesn't match the grain pattern I'm seeing. Is there any common phenomenon where high-quality hardwood behaves erratically like that during fine joinery?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
